3. vendor/ling_onesided/double_unc.py, routine pvand : John Burkardt, MIT
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

The routine pvand in double_unc.py is the Björck-Pereyra Vandermonde solver
as coded by John Burkardt in his VANDERMONDE library, run here in ball
arithmetic.

  Author    John Burkardt
  Code      pvand.m and vandermonde.c of the VANDERMONDE library,
            https://people.sc.fsu.edu/~jburkardt/m_src/vandermonde/pvand.m
            and
            https://people.sc.fsu.edu/~jburkardt/c_src/vandermonde/vandermonde.c
  License   The header of the routine reads: "Licensing: This code is
            distributed under the MIT license." (Modified: 14 November 2013;
            Author: John Burkardt.) The library carries no separate license
            file and no copyright line. The terms of the MIT License are
            those printed in the LICENSE file at the root of this repository;
            the copyright line printed there is that of BootLoops and not of
            John Burkardt.
  Method    A. Björck and V. Pereyra, "Solution of Vandermonde Systems of
            Equations", Math. Comp. 24 (1970) 893-903

What was taken. The loops and statements of pvand are those of Burkardt's
routine in its zero-based form, less the argument n.

Changes made. Translated to Python; every operation acts on Arb balls, so the
returned balls contain the exact solution.
